Title: "Readable files. Structured output."
One active global tab "Project files", plus another "Shell". Main content is a single terminal pane. Prompt tags "PowerShell" and "main"; path "./demo"; green lambda and "ls". Large dominant bordered table with five columns exactly "Type", "Name", "Size", "Modified", "Mode". Thin solid outer border, horizontal row separators, vertical column separators, clear header background and very subtle alternating navy row backgrounds. Seven data rows, each exactly aligned:
folder icon / "src" / "—" / "2026-01-02" / "d----";
folder icon / "assets" / "—" / "2026-01-02" / "d----";
orange code-file icon / "main.rs" / "4.1 KB" / "2026-01-03" / "-a---";
yellow braces-file icon / "package.json" / "1.2 KB" / "2026-01-03" / "-a---";
purple config-file icon / "settings.toml" / "2.0 KB" / "2026-01-04" / "-a---";
purple image-file icon / "coast.png" / "384 KB" / "2026-01-04" / "-a---";
blue document-file icon / "README.md" / "8.4 KB" / "2026-01-05" / "-a---".
Use colored distinct clean small glyphs for folder/code/config/image/document file types and corresponding subtle filename colors. Table occupies width without overflow; increase row padding enough to inspect all icons. After table show next green lambda cursor. External annotations: "File icons and colors make listings easier to scan" and "Borders, separators and alternating rows are configurable". Use no fake editor panels.

Title: "Read Kubernetes status at a glance."
One active global tab "Operations", inactive "Shell". One terminal pane. Small "PowerShell" tag. Path "./demo"; green lambda then exact command "kubectl get pods". Wide high-clarity bordered terminal table with exact columns "NAME", "READY", "STATUS", "RESTARTS", "AGE", and five fictional rows:
"api-demo" | "1/1" | "Running" | "0" | "12m";
"worker-demo" | "0/1" | "Running" | "0" | "2m";
"queue-demo" | "0/1" | "Pending" | "0" | "45s";
"job-demo" | "0/1" | "Completed" | "0" | "8m";
"cache-demo" | "0/1" | "CrashLoopBackOff" | "3" | "4m".
Status AND readiness colored accurately: api-demo Running and 1/1 GREEN; worker-demo Running and 0/1 AMBER; queue-demo Pending AMBER; job-demo Completed CYAN; cache-demo CrashLoopBackOff RED. Rest of cells calm gray. These are display colors of fictional CLI output, no cluster connection manager or remote widgets. Below table a small unobtrusive legend, externally styled and clearly separate from native terminal, "Green: ready   Amber: waiting / partial   Cyan: completed   Red: failure". Under output show idle green lambda. External annotations: "The same Running status can have different readiness" and "A successful kubectl command does not mean every pod is healthy". Bottom label "ILLUSTRATION • NOT A SCREENSHOT" must be clearly visible.
